This file compares wrapping and content-scope variants. It is not parsed by
the current Rocdown compiler. Decided article spelling is `:name` with
`[params]` (`syntax_v2_recommended.rocdown`). Wrapping examples below use that
form. Other prefixes are historical.

# Content scope

Markdown headings are already line-scoped. Block syntax should feel the same
when the body is one line.

## Headings

Markdown sugar (preferred for humans):

## Installing Rocci

Explicit block, line content:

:h2 Installing Rocci

Explicit block, section wrap (heavier than a heading needs):

:h2 {{Installing Rocci}}

Optional props, still line content:

:h2[id: "install"] Installing Rocci

## Short asides

Line content, no title:

:note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.

Params plus line content:

:caution[title: "Breaking"] The current compiler does not parse this file.

Params plus nested document:

:note[title: "Static pages"] {{
    First paragraph of the note.

    Second paragraph, with a [link](Guide.rocdown) and a fence:

    ```roc
    answer = 42
    ```
}}

Rejected mixed form (today's `@docs` body): params and Markdown in one `{ }`.

```text
:note {
    title: "Static pages"

    First paragraph of the note.
}
```

# Nested blocks

## Decided: bracket params, double-brace content

:tabs[group: "languages", kind: "language"] {{
    :tab[id: "roc", label: "Roc"] {{
        Roc tab. A `}` in this fence must not close the tab:

        ```roc
        pair = { a: 1, b: 2 }
        ```
    }}
    :tab[id: "rust", label: "Rust"] {{
        Rust tab.
    }}
}}

## Alternative: named closer for long or brace-heavy bodies

The closer follows the article prefix (`:end`). It is not `@end` and not a
`%` fence.

:tabs[group: "languages", kind: "language"]
    :tab[id: "roc", label: "Roc"]
        Roc tab. Closing is a line-start marker, not a brace count.

        ```roc
        pair = { a: 1, b: 2 }
        ```
    :end.tab
    :tab[id: "rust", label: "Rust"]
        Rust tab.
    :end.tab
:end.tabs

## Not recommended: single `{ }` mixing fields and nested `{{ }}`

:tabs {
    :tab {
        id: "tab1"
        label: "Tab 1"
        {{this is a tab content}}
    }
}

# Params-only blocks

:badge[label: "preview", tone: "preview"]

:img[src: "./img/yammi_banana.png", alt: "A banana"]

Long field lists still use article brackets, not `@page`-style `{ }`:

:img[src: "./img/yammi_banana.png", alt: "A banana", width: "50px"]

# Custom block types

@use "./Callout.rocci"

:callout[tone: "warn"] Don't copy this command.

# Prefix versus language class

Module and Rocci keep a single `@`. Article blocks use `:`.

@page { route: "/guides/syntax-v2/" }

@component Hello = |{ name }|
    <p>{name}</p>

## Decided: single colon, bracket params

:note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
:note[title: "Watch"] {{ Nested Markdown. }}

:tabs[group: "os"] {{
    :tab[id: "mac", label: "macOS"] {{
        Mac panel, including a fence with braces:

        ```roc
        pair = { a: 1, b: 2 }
        ```
    }}
}}

Parens are not used for article params (`:note(title: "Watch")` is out).

## Historical: `::` vs `!`

`::` (Vue-family; prefix only):

::note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
::note[title: "Watch"] {{ Nested Markdown. }}

`!` (prefix only; not a `%` closer):

!note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
!note[title: "Watch"] {{ Nested Markdown. }}

`![alt](url)` stays a Markdown image. `!note` is `!` plus an ident.

## Other prefixes (not selected)

.note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
/note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
+note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
\note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.

Same `@` (rejected: article class shares the language-island sigil):

@note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.
@note[title: "Watch"] {{ Nested Markdown. }}

`@@` as a doubled `@`:

@@note Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown.

`%note` as another punctuated prefix. No `%` end fence.

Not article blocks (stay Rocci / HTML islands):

<Hello name="Roc" />

Not this (looks like Rocci, fights document-root HTML islands):

```text
<Note title="Watch">Do not paste raw HTML.</Note>
```
